  "aciklama": "Tasman Bridge lost spans when a bulk carrier hit its piers. The cause: ship impact on unprotected piers outside the navigation span.\n\nFailure chain: Strong current → Ship leaves the main span → Hits two piers → Spans fall onto the ship → Cars drive into the gap\n\nRelated episode: Why the Tacoma Narrows Bridge Tore Itself Apart — https://youtu.be/qkzRUqlEy5I\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Tasman Bridge disaster 1975.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tasman_Bridge_disaster_1975.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Sydney Ferry in Hobart to assist following the 1975 collapse of the Tasman Bridge.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sydney_Ferry_in_Hobart_to_assist_following_the_1975_collapse_of_the_Tasman_Bridge.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Sydney ferries KOSCISUSKO and LADY FERGUSON boarded for trip to Hobart 1975.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sydney_ferries_KOSCISUSKO_and_LADY_FERGUSON_boarded_for_trip_to_Hobart_1975.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Tasman Bridge near Hobart, Tasmania, Australia b.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tasman_Bridge_near_Hobart%2C_Tasmania%2C_Australia_b.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Tasman Bridge disaster — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasman_Bridge_disaster\n• Government source — IP003 (cited by Wikipedia) — http://www.bitre.gov.au/publications/07/Files/IP003.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 27 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #TasmanBridge #bridges #history",
